{
  "counterfactual": {
    "what": "bench/rot/run.py driven with bettermemory.verify._COMMIT_DRIFT_ESCALATES monkeypatched to False. The shipped build has it True, so no DRIFT-ARM number here describes shipped behaviour. The shipped_default block does: it never reads the switch, so it is bit-identical to the control by construction, and the `result` and `control` keys below depend on exactly that.",
    "why": "The pre-registered flip condition that lived in a source comment above _COMMIT_DRIFT_ESCALATES fired (pooled.file_level_incumbent.ALL.alerts_per_catch = 3.4 >= 1.5 in multirepo-anchored-2026-07-30.json). This run measures the consequence the condition committed to, so the retraction is auditable rather than asserted.",
    "date": "2026-07-31",
    "switch": "_COMMIT_DRIFT_ESCALATES = False",
    "window": "the pinned window of bettermemory-60d-2026-07-26.json (t0 053ab9de, t1 388b5be7, --subdir src)",
    "control": "The same driver with the switch untouched reproduces bettermemory-60d-2026-07-26.json bit for bit on all three arms it published, on `detectors` and on `baselines`. The fourth arm, drift_only_relative_cite_anchored, postdates that artifact.",
    "result": "Every drift arm collapses onto never_flag: flag_rate 0.9674 -> 0.0, youden_j 0.0339 -> 0.0, unflagged_stale_rate 0.0 -> 1.0. shipped_default is bit-identical to the control, because the demotion branch in verdict_from_signals reads commit_drift_count directly and bypasses the switch.",
    "not_scored_by_the_convergence_guard": "Deliberately named outside test_bench_rot.py's bettermemory-*d-*.json glob. That guard asserts shipped_default == drift_only_relative_cite on every published run; this run separates them BY CONSTRUCTION, and sweeping it into the guard's corpus would either fail CI or force the guard to be loosened for a counterfactual."
  },
